       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. At that dose, the patient could have severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, peripheral edema, or shock. That risk applies even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe order also needs to come from a licensed prescriber. I can enter it once a clinician confirms the intended dose.\n\n- **If 5 mg was intended:** the usual starting dose is 2.5\u20135 mg by mouth once daily.\n- **If 10 mg was intended:** that is the maximum daily dose.\n\nThe prescribing clinician can give me the corrected dose, or confirm that 50 mg is intentional and add their rationale. I can then enter the order with that information in the note."
